  "id": "cognitive-deconstruction",
  "term": "cognitive deconstruction",
  "definition": "Cognitive deconstruction is a theory that, after painful experiences such as social exclusion, a person may defensively loosen their usual sense of self and reality. This state is linked to a fragmented mental experience and weaker cognitive functioning, including slower time perception and reduced self-control.",
